        "orario": "12:08",
        "timestamp": 1776593321,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. A petition called 'Lebanon will not be the next Gaza' calls on French leaders to take action Middle East Issued on: 19/04/2026 - 12:08 Modified: 19/04/2026 - 12:20 As France's President Emmanuel Macron is seen as a key guarantor of the ceasefire between Israel and Lebanon, civil society actors have launched a petition titled 'Lebanon will not be the next Gaza', calling on him to act. The initiative has been signed by numerous French public figures. Marie Yared, Senior Global Campaigner at the Avaaz Foundation, explains that the petition comes amid concerns that last year’s ceasefire was repeatedly violated by Israel, and urges European leaders to ensure the current truce holds to avoid a repeat of what happened in Gaza. Iran: Prolonged conflict reshapes view of the regime, analyst says 19/04/2026 Middle East Middle East: Hezbollah blamed after French peacekeeper killed in Lebanon 19/04/2026 Middle East What is UNIFIL? the UN mission in southern Lebanon explained 19/04/2026 Middle East Strait of Hormuz: Open, closed, open, closed - What's actually happening? 18/04/2026 Middle East Replay : Donald Trump holds briefing amid Hormuz tension 18/04/2026 Middle East UNIFIL sheds light on southern Lebanon attack that killed French soldier 18/04/2026 Middle East No signs of regime collapse as Iran weathers weeks of war 18/04/2026 Middle East Hormuz tensions highlight pressure tactics in US-Iran negotiations 18/04/2026 Middle East Turkey’s economy hit as Syrians return home 18/04/2026 Middle East"
