        "orario": "13:36",
        "timestamp": 1776598580,
        "contenuto_esteso": "2 Updates Auto-updates live-orange 10m ago ( 11:50 GMT ) How have City performed in recent weeks? While Arsenal have stuttered, City are approaching top gear, having beaten Arsenal, Liverpool and Chelsea in their last three games in all competitions. City sit second in the league with 64 points from 31 games, with Pep Guardiola’s rejuvenated side knowing that victory over Arsenal in Sunday’s showdown would make them favourites to reclaim the crown. While City have not lost at home to Arsenal in the league for 11 years, Arsenal are also unbeaten in their last five Premier League games against City. live-orange 25m ago ( 11:35 GMT ) Welcome to our live coverage Hello, welcome and thanks for joining our live coverage as Manchester City host Arsenal in a crucial top-of-the-table clash in the Premier League. Under-pressue league leaders Arsenal are bracing for their most challenging game in recent weeks as they travel to the Etihad Stadium. Man City are enjoying a late surge of form and momentum as they look to turn the tables on the Londoners. Aiming for their first league title since 2003-04, Arsenal were the frontrunners for the trophy for most part of the season but a recent dip in form has thrown the title race wide open. After suffering only three defeats in their opening 49 matches of the season in all competitions, Arsenal have lost three of their past four, ramping up the pressure on the visitors. Today’s fixture could turn out to be a potential title decider, as the season enters its tail end. I’m Hafsa Adil, and I’ll take you through our live build-up to the match along with all the photo coverage of the day. Rohan Sharma will bring you the team sheets as they drop, as well as comprehensive text commentary of the game. A six-point margin. A Premier League title on the line. It doesn't get much bigger than this. @ManCity host @Arsenal — Premier League (@premierleague) April 12, 2026"
